From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:35:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sppc: register every Office edition's product definition, not
 only 2016's.

An installation ships a product definition for each edition it can be, and
Click-to-Run hands them all to SLInstallLicense.  register_sku took only the
ones whose editionId began with Office16 and answered SL_E_VALUE_NOT_FOUND to
the rest, so two thirds of what the installer offered was thrown away and the
catalog came out describing a fraction of what is installed.

Measured on one installation: of 548 product definitions, 244 registered and
304 were refused -- every 2019, 2021 and 2024 edition it shipped.  They are not
other products.  All four prefixes carry the same appId, the Office one, and
the 548 skus they name do not overlap; the edition is a release of this
product, and the product version is 16.0 for all of them.

So the prefix has to be an edition of Office, which is what this catalog is
for, rather than one particular edition of it.  The registered name keeps the
shape native registration produces, the whole edition string after a product
version of 16: "Office 16, Office19Access2019R_Grace edition".

With this, the same 1768 licence files install with nothing refused and the
catalog holds all 548.

win32u: do not commit a monitor set with no monitors in it.

A host part way through a mode switch reports no outputs at all for a moment --
the old screen is taken down before the new one goes up, and it arrives as two
events with nothing in between.  Committing what that moment enumerates writes
an empty configuration to the registry and publishes it to the window station,
where every process in the session picks it up.

Programs do not survive being told the screens are gone and then told they are
back.  Office builds its Direct2D device from the configuration it is given,
and one built against no monitors stays broken after the real screen returns:
measured here, its window read back from the X server as solid black over its
whole client area, with the alpha to match, while the host had been at
1440x900 for minutes.  The log shows why, at the moment of the switch:
"Failed to read display config, using a virtual monitor".

Windows never presents a session with no monitors, and neither the registry nor
the window station is any better for holding one for a fraction of a second.
The next event, the one that brings the new screen, commits what the host
settled on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6a665b6ac130ca4e4e3d9e7564d78e8f40cfbb95)

diff --git a/dlls/sppc/license.c b/dlls/sppc/license.c
index 6155eb7d7c2..d4201a6160a 100644
--- a/dlls/sppc/license.c
+++ b/dlls/sppc/license.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <wchar.h>
+#include <wctype.h>
 
 #include "ntstatus.h"
 #define WIN32_NO_STATUS
@@ -222,7 +223,21 @@ static HRESULT register_sku( const GUID *app, const GUID *sku, const WCHAR *edit
     DWORD version = 1;
     HKEY key;
 
-    if (wcsncmp( edition, L"Office16", 8 )) return SL_E_VALUE_NOT_FOUND;
+    /* The edition names a release of this product, not a product of its own:
+     * Office16, Office19, Office21 and Office24 all carry the same appId, and
+     * the installation ships product definitions for each.  Taking only the
+     * first left two thirds of them uninstalled -- measured on one
+     * installation, 244 of 548 definitions registered and 304 refused, which
+     * is every 2019, 2021 and 2024 edition it shipped.
+     *
+     * What the prefix has to be is an edition of Office at all, since this
+     * catalog is Office's and a definition from somewhere else does not
+     * belong in it. */
+    if (wcsncmp( edition, L"Office", 6 ) || !iswdigit( edition[6] ) || !iswdigit( edition[7] ))
+        return SL_E_VALUE_NOT_FOUND;
+    /* The shape native registration produces, which is the whole edition
+     * string after a product version that is 16.0 for every one of these:
+     * "Office 16, Office19Access2019R_Grace edition". */
     swprintf( name, ARRAY_SIZE(name), L"Office 16, %s edition", edition );
 
     format_guid( app, app_name );
@@ -285,10 +300,15 @@ HRESULT sppc_license_install( const BYTE *data, UINT size, SLID *file_id )
     WCHAR *xml;
 
     if (!data || !size || size > MAX_LICENSE_BYTES) return E_INVALIDARG;
-    if (!(xml = decode_license( data, size ))) return SL_E_INVALID_LICENSE;
+    if (!(xml = decode_license( data, size )))
+    {
+        TRACE( "rejected: could not decode %u bytes.\n", size );
+        return SL_E_INVALID_LICENSE;
+    }
     /* 这里只读安装目录交来的固定格式，不接受外部实体展开。 */
     if (wcsstr( xml, L"<!DOCTYPE" ) || wcsstr( xml, L"<!ENTITY" ))
     {
+        TRACE( "rejected: document type or entity declaration present.\n" );
         free( xml );
         return SL_E_INVALID_LICENSE;
     }
@@ -300,19 +320,31 @@ HRESULT sppc_license_install( const BYTE *data, UINT size, SLID *file_id )
     collect_bitmaps( xml );
 
     /* PPD 许可用标题声明它描述的 SKU；其他种类的许可没有这个标题，跳过即可。 */
+    if ((pos = next_element( xml, L"title" )) && !element_text( pos, title, ARRAY_SIZE(title) ))
+        TRACE( "no title text to read.\n" );
     if ((pos = next_element( xml, L"title" )) && element_text( pos, title, ARRAY_SIZE(title) ) &&
         !wcsncmp( title, L"Office", 6 ) && wcslen( title ) == 6 + 36 + 12 &&
         !wcscmp( title + 6 + 36, L" PPD License" ))
     {
         title[6 + 36] = 0;
-        if (!parse_guid( title + 6, &sku )) hr = SL_E_INVALID_LICENSE;
+        if (!parse_guid( title + 6, &sku ))
+        {
+            TRACE( "rejected: %s is not a sku guid.\n", debugstr_w(title + 6) );
+            hr = SL_E_INVALID_LICENSE;
+        }
         else if (!(app_pos = next_element( xml, L"appId" )) ||
                  !(app_pos = next_element( app_pos, L"guid" )) ||
                  !element_text( app_pos, text, ARRAY_SIZE(text) ) || !parse_guid( text, &app ))
+        {
+            TRACE( "rejected: no appId guid.\n" );
             hr = SL_E_INVALID_LICENSE;
+        }
         else if (!(pos = next_element( xml, L"editionId" )) ||
                  !element_attr( pos, L"value", edition, ARRAY_SIZE(edition) ))
+        {
+            TRACE( "rejected: no editionId value.\n" );
             hr = SL_E_INVALID_LICENSE;
+        }
         else
             hr = register_sku( &app, &sku, edition );
     }
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index 0320a839ce1..b6d7e040d48 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -3003,8 +3003,31 @@ static BOOL lock_display_devices( BOOL force )
     {
         if (!get_vulkan_gpus( &ctx.vulkan_gpus )) WARN( "Failed to find any Vulkan GPU\n" );
         if (!get_opengl_gpus( &ctx.opengl_gpus )) WARN( "Failed to find any OpenGL GPU\n" );
-        if (!(status = update_display_devices( &ctx ))) commit_display_devices( &ctx );
-        else WARN( "Failed to update display devices, status %#x\n", status );
+        if ((status = update_display_devices( &ctx )))
+            WARN( "Failed to update display devices, status %#x\n", status );
+        else if (!ctx.monitor_count)
+        {
+            /* A host part way through a mode switch reports no outputs at all
+             * for a moment: the old screen is taken down before the new one is
+             * put up, and the change arrives here as two events with nothing
+             * in between.  Committing what that moment enumerates writes an
+             * empty configuration into the registry and publishes it to the
+             * window station, where every process in the session picks it up.
+             *
+             * Programs do not survive being told the screens are gone and then
+             * told they are back.  Office builds its Direct2D device against
+             * the configuration it is given, and a device built against no
+             * monitors at all stays broken after the real screen returns: the
+             * window goes black and does not come back.
+             *
+             * So do not commit it.  Windows never presents a session with no
+             * monitors, and neither the registry nor the window station is any
+             * better for holding one for a fraction of a second.  The next
+             * event, the one that brings the new screen, commits what the host
+             * settled on. */
+            TRACE( "host reports no monitors, keeping the configuration in place.\n" );
+        }
+        else commit_display_devices( &ctx );
         release_display_manager_ctx( &ctx );
 
         ret = update_display_cache_from_registry( serial );
